<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anna of Kashin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1280–1368</span> · Also known as Saint Anna of Kashin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anna of Kashin was a Russian princess, wife of Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-of-tver">Mikhail of Tver</a>, who was executed at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> in 1318. Two of her sons were also killed by the Horde. In old age she became a nun and lived in Kashin, where she died. She was venerated as a saint, and her cult, suppressed in the late 17th century, was restored in 1909.</p></div>
